p.src:
Choose, for example, $(\sigma,\nu,\tau)=(y,x,0).$ Then Equation  combines two spatial derivatives of electric components with a time derivative of a magnetic component: $\partial_yF_{x0}
+
\partial_xF_{0y}
+
\partial_0F_{yx}
=0.$ Using the matrix in Equation , this is one component of $\boldsymbol\nabla\times\mathbf E
-\frac{\partial\mathbf B}{\partial t}
=\mathbf0,$ with the relative signs fixed by antisymmetry. Choosing the other pairs of spatial indices supplies the other two curl components.

